# ImmichFrame is configured in the admin editor at /admin, not through this file.
#
# To bring an existing configuration along, mount a Settings.json, Settings.yml or
# Settings.yaml into the config directory. It is imported into the settings database
# on first start and ignored afterwards. See docker/Settings.example.json for the
# format. Configuration from environment variables is not imported — settings that
# used to live in this file have to be migrated by hand.
#
# The variables below are the only ones ImmichFrame still reads from the environment.

# Where the settings database and an optional Settings.json/yml live.
# Defaults to a "Config" directory next to the executable.
# IMMICHFRAME_CONFIG_PATH=/app/Config

# Trace | Debug | Information | Warning | Error | Critical
# LOG_LEVEL=Information

# Timezone used for clock and calendar display.
TZ=Europe/Berlin

# --- Admin configuration editor (optional) ---
# Environment only, never Settings.json/Settings.yml or the settings database - the editor must not
# be able to lock you out of itself, and the client secret stays out of the configuration it writes.
# Leave any of the first three unset and the admin surface is off: every admin endpoint answers 404
# except the one that reports it is off.
# IMMICHFRAME_OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://idp.example.com/realms/immichframe
# IMMICHFRAME_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=immichframe
# IMMICHFRAME_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Comma-separated administrators. Each entry is compared against both the 'sub' and the 'email'
# claims of whoever signs in, and a match on either grants access. An empty or missing list means
# nobody - it never means everyone - so the admin surface stays off until you name someone.
# Prefer 'sub' on anything but a single-tenant identity provider you control. An email entry is
# refused only when the provider explicitly reports email_verified=false; if the provider omits that
# claim, ImmichFrame cannot tell a verified address from one the user typed into their own profile,
# so on a provider with open registration an email entry can be claimed by a stranger. A 'sub' is
# assigned by the provider and can never be chosen by the user.
# IMMICHFRAME_OIDC_ADMINS=admin@example.com,00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# Set to true only when a reverse proxy in front of ImmichFrame sets X-Forwarded-Proto/Host.
# Without it, a TLS-terminating proxy makes ImmichFrame build an http:// redirect_uri that your
# identity provider will reject; with it on and no proxy in front, a client can forge those headers.
# IMMICHFRAME_OIDC_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=false
